# CODEOWNERS — last matching pattern wins
# platform-as-iac-repo (ADR "Zone isolation in IaC"). Each owner team is created by create-teams.sh with its
# own write grant on platform-as-iac-repo, or GitHub ignores it. GitHub accepts one approval from any owner
# listed on a line; the Run apply adds the second person (environment "run").

# Everything not listed below: the CoE platform lead (owner of the ADR)
*                       @platform-team/coe-platform-lead

# From the ADR
/zones/control-plane/   @platform-team/coe-squad-a-lead
/zones/run/             @platform-team/coe-squad-b-lead @platform-team/coe-security
/bootstrap/             @platform-team/coe-squad-b-lead @platform-team/coe-security

# Not in the ADR. These files decide what Build and Run receive (published/), the checks that prove
# C1-C12 (policy/), and what the pipelines run with zone credentials (.github/, scripts/): a change
# there reaches Run as surely as a change in zones/run/.
/published/             @platform-team/coe-squad-a-lead
/policy/                @platform-team/coe-security
/.github/               @platform-team/coe-squad-b-lead @platform-team/coe-security
/scripts/               @platform-team/coe-squad-b-lead @platform-team/coe-security
/CODEOWNERS             @platform-team/coe-security
